.TH LEGION 1 "2026" "legion" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
legion \- remote control node and CLI for managing machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B legion
.I tool
[\fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR ...] [\fB\-\-args\fR \fIJSON\fR|\fB\-\fR]
[\fB\-\-on\fR \fImachine\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR \fIprincipal\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B help
[\fItool\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B tools
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B init
[\fB\-\-name\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-roles\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B cp
.I from to
[\fB\-\-delete\fR] [\fB\-\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B pair
\fB\-\-as\fR \fIprincipal\fR [\fB\-\-valid\fR \fI15m\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIhost\fR]... [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.br
.B legion
.B serve
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIaddress\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B legion
is a single executable that exposes the same set of system, file, command,
background job, service, project, power, and fleet tools on every machine over
the command line, SSH (\fBlegion rpc\fR), MCP (\fBlegion mcp\fR), and a
loopback HTTP server (\fBlegion serve\fR).
.PP
Every call is checked against the node's policy and recorded in an append-only
audit log.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B legion init
Create starter \fInode.toml\fR and \fIpolicy.toml\fR files where they do not
already exist.
.TP
.B legion tools
List every tool registered on this node, including local extensions in
\fItools.d/\fR.
.TP
.B legion help \fR[\fItool\fR]
Show usage or the full description and argument schema for one tool.
.TP
.B legion \fItool\fR \fR[\fIkey\fR=\fIvalue\fR ...]
Run a tool locally, or on another machine named in \fIfleet.toml\fR with
\fB\-\-on\fR \fImachine\fR (or \fB\-\-on all\fR).
.TP
.B legion cp \fIfrom to\fR
Copy a file or directory tree between machines with resume and sync support.
.TP
.B legion pair \fB\-\-as\fR \fIprincipal\fR
Create a time-limited pairing invite for a mobile or remote client and display
it as a QR code and text token.
.TP
.B legion serve
Serve the built-in web interface and the node's tools over HTTP on loopback
only (127.0.0.1:7117 by default).
.TP
.B legion rpc\fR, \fBlegion mcp\fR, \fBlegion stream\fR, \fBlegion gate
Protocol endpoints for SSH transport, AI agents, bulk file transfers, and
restricted SSH keys.
.TP
.B legion agents\fR, \fBlegion token
Register the MCP server with coding agents, or manage bearer tokens for
\fBlegion serve\fR.
.TP
.B legion \-\-version
Print the installed version and build revision.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/legion/
Configuration directory (or \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/legion\fR): \fInode.toml\fR,
\fIfleet.toml\fR, \fIpolicy.toml\fR, \fIprojects.toml\fR, \fItokens.toml\fR,
and \fItools.d/*.toml\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/legion/
State directory (or \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/legion\fR): \fIaudit.jsonl\fR,
\fIdevices.json\fR, \fIjobs/\fR, and \fIsync/\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/legion\-serve.service
Optional systemd user unit for \fBlegion serve\fR (not enabled by default).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEGION_HOME
Override both configuration and state directories with
\fI$LEGION_HOME/config\fR and \fI$LEGION_HOME/state\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
Run \fBlegion help\fR for full CLI usage and \fBlegion tools\fR for every tool.
Project homepage: https://github.com/x1f4r/legion-control
